# Reproducer 7: Exported Struct Fields Lower as Private Across Modules
# Category: Module/interface projection problem
# Command: margo build (with two modules in separate files)
#
# Observed behavior:
# When `module A` defines `export type Data: x: Int`, and `module B` creates an
# instance `A.Data(x: 10)`, native compilation fails with rustc error[E0451]:
# "field `x` of struct `moss_A::A__Data` is private"
#
# Root Cause:
# Lowering emits `pub struct A__Data { x: i64 }` where the struct is `pub` but its
# fields omit `pub`. Across Rust crate boundaries, Rust forbids struct literal
# construction when fields are private.

# In module Provider:
module Provider

export type Data:
  value: Int

# In module Consumer:
module Consumer
import Provider

fn main():
  d = Provider.Data(value: 42)
  echo d.value
